WEBVTT

00:07.040 --> 00:09.110
The tea I promised.

00:11.330 --> 00:14.030
My, my. You have excellent taste.

00:14.500 --> 00:16.790
From our Ildoan friends?

00:17.820 --> 00:20.750
We must be grateful for 
our allies' friendship.

00:21.260 --> 00:23.290
For the moment, at least.

00:24.610 --> 00:27.000
Once again, I thank you for your support.

00:27.000 --> 00:29.910
Well done, as always, 
Lt. Colonel Degurechaff.

00:29.910 --> 00:33.900
You did everything you possibly could 
to support the main offensive.

00:33.900 --> 00:37.620
I simply threw my soldiers' lives 
into the enemy's gaping maw.

00:37.620 --> 00:39.800
No talent was needed on my part.

00:39.800 --> 00:43.660
Which implies that the fault lies 
with the man who gave the order?

00:43.660 --> 00:45.660
A fascinatingly biting remark, that.

00:45.660 --> 00:51.060
In my position, it's best for me to 
respect formality and say nothing.

00:51.060 --> 00:53.430
You never change.

00:53.430 --> 00:55.570
You never, ever change.

00:55.570 --> 00:58.050
I believe in myself.

00:59.400 --> 01:02.110
<i>And I always follow my own path.</i>

01:02.740 --> 01:06.820
<i>Rather than entrust my fate 
to people like Being X,</i>

01:06.820 --> 01:09.580
<i>I believe in my own right 
to make decisions.</i>

01:09.580 --> 01:13.390
<i>As a person living in modern times, 
I take pride in that.</i>

01:13.920 --> 01:18.160
I hate to interrupt our fancy 
tea party, but I have bad news.

01:19.340 --> 01:21.950
Andromeda has failed.

01:22.860 --> 01:26.680
Th-They weren't able to 
make it past the southern cities?

01:27.100 --> 01:29.370
They didn't even make it that far.

01:29.370 --> 01:32.780
They were able to make a lightning 
strike all the way to Josephgrad,

01:33.070 --> 01:35.340
but then their supply lines broke down.

01:35.340 --> 01:37.890
And the Federation Army 
strengthened its defenses.

01:37.890 --> 01:39.790
They can't go any further.

01:39.790 --> 01:43.000
Then the resource-rich areas 
we were targeting...

01:43.290 --> 01:45.650
They'll never make it.

03:17.500 --> 03:22.470
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

03:23.700 --> 03:25.240
I'm surprised.

03:25.240 --> 03:28.220
General Rudersdorf 
doesn't fail like that often...

03:28.560 --> 03:32.220
He didn't get the supplies 
he needed, I assume.

03:32.220 --> 03:34.980
The railways department did the 
best they could, it seems, but...

03:34.980 --> 03:38.440
So I was right, and we just didn't 
have enough supplies at all?

03:39.170 --> 03:41.190
That is my assumption.

03:43.440 --> 03:47.700
Not enough men, not enough food, 
not enough ammunition.

03:48.010 --> 03:53.720
While I was at HQ, it was my job to 
make things work with what we had.

03:54.350 --> 04:00.710
I heard that you were sent here after 
an argument with High Leadership.

04:00.710 --> 04:01.710
Correct.

04:01.970 --> 04:05.300
Do the people back home 
not know the truth?

04:05.300 --> 04:06.520
Lt. Colonel...

04:07.140 --> 04:09.970
The Empire is addicted to victory.

04:09.970 --> 04:11.530
It's almost sad.

04:13.540 --> 04:17.840
We must be victorious 
in the battles within.

04:17.840 --> 04:22.200
And for that, we're going to have 
to learn to do the unpleasant.

04:23.470 --> 04:26.200
Sir, you do mean...

04:26.750 --> 04:29.360
If we're to be able to focus on the east,

04:29.360 --> 04:32.380
we must be victorious in the 
battles to the west, as well.

04:32.680 --> 04:37.620
By the west, are you referring 
to the western air war?

04:38.990 --> 04:42.680
A little further to the 
east than that, actually.

04:43.210 --> 04:45.390
<i>I knew it...</i>

04:45.390 --> 04:48.800
<i>I'd rather not shoot my own allies 
if I could avoid it, but...</i>

04:50.700 --> 04:55.440
I'm going to ask you to 
be my co-conspirator.

04:58.220 --> 05:02.780
If I may, I am a soldier of the Empire.

05:02.780 --> 05:08.570
I am a part of a military organization, 
and I have a duty to follow lawful orders.

05:08.880 --> 05:10.850
I cannot betray my duty.

05:11.220 --> 05:16.380
Doing so would be treason against 
both the army and the Imperial family.

05:16.380 --> 05:18.330
I will fulfill my duty.

05:19.540 --> 05:22.430
Neither a yes nor a no, huh?

05:25.040 --> 05:26.970
Wonderful.

05:26.970 --> 05:31.420
Any other answer, and I would 
have been forced to kill you.

05:32.790 --> 05:37.050
You seem to be laboring 
under a misapprehension.

05:39.030 --> 05:40.340
Well, whatever.

05:40.340 --> 05:43.700
First, you need to see 
what it's like back home.

05:43.700 --> 05:45.510
See the reality of the Empire.

05:45.940 --> 05:49.950
<b>Episode Seven
Purgatory</b>

05:49.950 --> 05:54.040
<b>June 29, Unified Year 1927</b>

05:56.540 --> 05:57.850
We're here!

05:57.850 --> 05:59.490
Time for leave!

06:02.700 --> 06:04.250
Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff!

06:04.510 --> 06:06.510
Welcome back!

06:06.510 --> 06:10.300
Colonel! You've returned as well, I see.

06:10.300 --> 06:13.900
The Rerugen Combat Team 
is on leave back in the capital.

06:13.900 --> 06:16.150
It makes sense for me to be here.

06:16.150 --> 06:17.730
You're right.

06:18.430 --> 06:23.190
Everyone! I've prepared 
a resort for our leave!

06:25.080 --> 06:27.440
May I speak to you, Lieutenant Colonel?

06:28.790 --> 06:32.520
Major Weiss, prepare the leave 
certificates and coupons.

06:32.520 --> 06:34.680
Lieutenant Serebryakov, prepare the cars.

06:34.680 --> 06:35.490
Ma'am!

06:36.510 --> 06:39.550
I will now distribute 
your leave certificates and coupons!

06:39.830 --> 06:41.030
Everyone, line up!

06:41.560 --> 06:44.450
I trust them completely, but...

06:44.450 --> 06:46.890
It's necessary.

06:47.530 --> 06:49.880
For now, let me tell you three things.

06:49.880 --> 06:50.810
Yes, sir.

06:51.120 --> 06:55.290
First, Strategic HQ and High Leadership
 are in an uproar over

06:55.290 --> 06:59.330
who takes responsibility for the failure
 of the large-scale offensive in the East.

07:00.830 --> 07:04.140
The army is being asked 
for the impossible again.

07:04.140 --> 07:08.530
"End the war immediately. 
With an incredible victory."

07:08.850 --> 07:12.980
I see. Then we need complete 
air superiority in the east.

07:13.280 --> 07:15.020
And that's the second thing.

07:15.020 --> 07:18.730
The air situation in the west 
has badly deteriorated.

07:18.730 --> 07:21.630
We're looking at pulling back 
forces not just from the east,

07:21.630 --> 07:23.670
but the southern continent as well.

07:24.340 --> 07:26.380
It's that bad?

07:26.380 --> 07:28.250
And one last thing.

07:28.730 --> 07:32.260
We may have you do an air raid 
on another capital.

07:33.570 --> 07:36.250
A direct strike on Londinium?

07:36.250 --> 07:37.800
No, not there.

07:38.240 --> 07:40.130
Another strike on Moskva, then?

07:40.580 --> 07:42.650
No, Lieutenant Colonel.

07:43.730 --> 07:45.040
Your target will be...

07:55.560 --> 07:58.150
No, I won't say it here.

07:58.430 --> 08:01.970
You won an incredible victory 
during Operation Iron Hammer.

08:01.970 --> 08:06.660
At the time, I was part of 
the peace negotiations in Ildoa...

08:09.270 --> 08:11.250
That was the real goal.

08:12.060 --> 08:16.920
If only those damn politicians would've 
accepted the military's peace proposal.

08:21.270 --> 08:27.260
<i>So if we want to change things, 
we need to wake up the politicians?</i>

08:33.950 --> 08:41.200
<b>Imperial Strategic HQ</b>

08:37.290 --> 08:38.990
Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff.

08:38.990 --> 08:41.190
I've come to receive new orders.

08:41.470 --> 08:43.490
It's been a while, Lieutenant Colonel.

08:43.490 --> 08:45.700
I'm glad to see you're doing well.

08:46.170 --> 08:48.210
It seems you're doing well too, sir.

08:49.370 --> 08:52.750
I keep getting stuck with 
more useless work, but yes.

08:53.210 --> 08:56.220
You did excellent work in the east.

08:56.220 --> 09:00.990
Still, I apologize for my unit's 
difficulties during Project Andromeda.

09:00.990 --> 09:03.110
We can skip the formalities.

09:03.650 --> 09:07.470
No matter the reason, the fact 
that I failed doesn't change.

09:07.850 --> 09:12.660
And that's why I want your honest 
opinion as a frontline officer.

09:12.660 --> 09:13.570
Yes, sir.

09:13.980 --> 09:17.190
At a minimum, we managed 
to reorganize the battle lines.

09:17.190 --> 09:19.070
But that's not enough.

09:19.070 --> 09:22.980
Merely stopping the bleeding 
won't be enough to win.

09:23.530 --> 09:25.840
Over the long term, we may be forced 
to make unavoidable decisions...

09:25.840 --> 09:26.780
Stop.

09:27.120 --> 09:29.520
I'm not Zettour.

09:29.520 --> 09:32.760
I don't have his bad habit of enjoying 
long speeches during debates.

09:33.210 --> 09:36.630
Your conclusion. I want 
your conclusion first.

09:36.630 --> 09:40.770
Sir, I am simply a mage 
and a lieutenant colonel.

09:40.770 --> 09:43.100
I completed the strategy 
curriculum during training,

09:43.100 --> 09:45.190
but I've spent too long 
on the front lines.

09:46.430 --> 09:48.360
Your conclusion, or you leave the room.

09:48.360 --> 09:49.290
Choose.

09:51.280 --> 09:55.020
All right.
I will defer to your preference.

09:55.020 --> 09:57.930
I see no way to win this war.

09:58.300 --> 10:02.650
No one on the front lines understands 
how command intends to fight this war.

10:02.650 --> 10:08.070
How do we intend to end it? Do we 
have any practical plan to do so?

10:08.070 --> 10:10.670
Are we to destroy the enemy's field army?

10:10.670 --> 10:13.790
Occupy their important cities?

10:13.790 --> 10:15.430
What is our goal?

10:15.760 --> 10:20.410
What goal is the Empire, 
as a nation, pursuing?

10:21.650 --> 10:23.110
Victory.

10:23.470 --> 10:29.190
"Victory"? But to end this war, 
what kind of victory are we to—

10:28.480 --> 10:29.750
Victory.

10:30.270 --> 10:32.970
Nothing more. Nothing less.

10:33.310 --> 10:34.700
So...

10:34.700 --> 10:37.990
The military's only been 
ordered to bring "victory"?

10:38.250 --> 10:39.990
Correct.

10:41.360 --> 10:44.990
Is that... so?

10:45.790 --> 10:51.700
So High Leadership is incapable of even 
coming up with a concrete objective?

10:52.060 --> 10:53.760
Correct.

10:53.760 --> 10:55.840
But that's ridiculous...

10:55.840 --> 10:57.500
Correct.

10:57.850 --> 11:01.810
If it weren't for the fools 
who deprived us of the option to quit,

11:01.810 --> 11:05.140
this war would've been over 
a long time ago.

11:05.350 --> 11:08.690
We can cry. We can pray. 
But that will not change.

11:08.690 --> 11:12.390
Colonel Rerugen looked 
very tired as well.

11:12.390 --> 11:16.090
How do we make the leadership 
understand reality?

11:16.580 --> 11:19.910
You seem to be misunderstanding.

11:20.640 --> 11:25.400
Is this what they call missing 
the forest for the trees?

11:25.800 --> 11:29.730
Lieutenant Colonel, 
the politicians at High Leadership

11:29.730 --> 11:33.840
are living, breathing human beings, 
and they're afraid of public opinion.

11:34.200 --> 11:38.420
Public opinion is like lava. And they 
don't want it to get trapped in it.

11:38.420 --> 11:40.140
Public opinion?

11:40.600 --> 11:44.410
Yes. You've spent your whole 
young life as a soldier.

11:44.410 --> 11:48.000
You've never lived anywhere 
but the front lines,

11:48.000 --> 11:49.970
so perhaps this is strange to you.

11:51.600 --> 11:53.040
Hmm...

11:53.040 --> 11:56.030
You need to see what the capital 
is like right now for yourself

11:56.030 --> 11:59.630
and learn how the public feels, it seems.

12:00.390 --> 12:04.290
Be at the plaza in front of 
Central Station at 1500 tomorrow.

12:04.880 --> 12:07.890
I'll have my attendants 
make preparations.

12:10.460 --> 12:13.540
Is that what General Rudersdorf said?

12:13.540 --> 12:16.350
Yes. I was a little surprised...

12:16.350 --> 12:19.050
His old boldness was still there, but...

12:19.050 --> 12:21.660
How do I even describe it?

12:21.660 --> 12:26.500
You can see part of what 
he mentioned right now.

12:27.720 --> 12:30.310
Lieutenant Colonel Uger, this is...

12:30.700 --> 12:33.050
Herb tea. Very popular right now.

12:33.050 --> 12:35.210
Good for your health, they say.

12:38.790 --> 12:41.720
I won't deny that health is important,

12:41.720 --> 12:45.680
but as a civilized woman, 
I'd want some caffeine.

12:45.680 --> 12:47.300
Here you are.

12:49.740 --> 12:52.060
<i>War sausage and K-Brot?</i>

12:52.410 --> 12:58.070
This cafeteria is known for its good food.
I didn't expect it to be like this.

12:58.070 --> 13:01.290
Everything back home is substitutes, 
because the real stuff

13:01.290 --> 13:03.250
is going to the front lines.

13:04.660 --> 13:05.870
My, my...

13:05.870 --> 13:09.920
A full-on war is a scary thing, huh?

13:10.660 --> 13:14.010
But it's not that much to ask.

13:14.010 --> 13:19.070
During wartime,
 they'll just have to put up with it.

13:21.790 --> 13:22.980
Lieutenant Colonel...

13:23.800 --> 13:26.190
I'd like to make you a proposal.

13:27.170 --> 13:29.650
I don't want you to 
take this the wrong way,

13:29.650 --> 13:33.830
but I'd like you to understand 
how human beings feel.

13:34.140 --> 13:39.580
In a broader sense, I'd like you 
to behave like a normal person.

13:40.200 --> 13:41.170
Are you...

13:41.380 --> 13:44.960
Are you doubting my character?

13:44.960 --> 13:47.470
I certainly don't intend to insult you!

13:47.470 --> 13:48.670
Please understand that.

13:51.690 --> 13:57.430
But you're always too quick to seek 
an immediate answer for things.

13:57.430 --> 14:00.730
Which leads you to disrespect those 
who are incapable of doing so.

14:01.120 --> 14:03.590
Emotions are a stubborn thing.

14:03.590 --> 14:08.330
To loosen them up requires time.

14:09.180 --> 14:11.490
I understand how you feel.

14:11.490 --> 14:15.050
But need requires reason.

14:15.050 --> 14:18.440
A lack of firm resolve leads 
to missed opportunities

14:18.440 --> 14:20.400
and is nothing more than a hindrance.

14:20.840 --> 14:22.060
That's what I'm talking about.

14:22.440 --> 14:24.870
I can't understand how your mind works.

14:24.870 --> 14:28.890
Not everyone can live 
their lives the way you do.

14:29.160 --> 14:32.150
I'm an adult. I've lived a long time.

14:32.150 --> 14:35.560
As an Imperial strategist, I've undergone 
training in the military code as well.

14:35.920 --> 14:37.460
And yet...

14:37.880 --> 14:41.650
Right now, I'm like a little child.

14:42.050 --> 14:44.430
I want to cry more than anything!

14:45.650 --> 14:47.490
Lieutenant Colonel...

14:47.490 --> 14:52.570
I can't continue being the monster 
that a strategist needs to be.

14:53.110 --> 14:55.920
I'm sure things started to change 
when my daughter was born.

14:56.500 --> 15:01.910
To be honest, I thank you 
for suggesting I serve in the rear.

15:01.910 --> 15:05.410
I'm a soldier, and this is how I feel.

15:05.410 --> 15:11.180
Tomorrow, you'll see 
how exhausted the Empire is.

15:11.960 --> 15:14.460
What reality is like in the capital.

15:18.920 --> 15:22.900
<i>To think I'm being called to 
a ceremony for fallen soldiers...</i>

15:23.610 --> 15:26.200
<i>If the general and I had come 
here in our military uniforms,</i>

15:26.200 --> 15:28.200
<i>we would've stood out, in a bad way.</i>

15:28.200 --> 15:31.190
<i>I'm lucky he prepared 
this funeral outfit for me.</i>

15:43.660 --> 15:44.910
You can't see?

15:45.300 --> 15:48.470
U-Um, I'm not tall enough...

15:48.860 --> 15:52.520
Given where we are, I can't 
put you on my shoulders.

15:53.950 --> 15:57.100
Excuse me. Would you 
please allow her to see?

16:01.650 --> 16:03.380
Look at them.

16:04.570 --> 16:07.570
Those coffins don't have bodies in them.

16:08.060 --> 16:10.560
Even if they're just pretending 
the coffin is heavy...

16:11.730 --> 16:14.330
It's a horrible thing to see.

16:14.850 --> 16:17.520
Is this what you were talking about?

16:17.910 --> 16:19.410
Yes.

16:19.410 --> 16:22.760
The sick and the young, 
carrying the coffins of the dead.

16:23.280 --> 16:27.830
There's no better way to describe 
the current state of the Empire.

16:29.510 --> 16:32.640
But there's more to the story than that.

16:33.070 --> 16:35.710
Look at the faces of 
the people around you.

17:20.150 --> 17:23.420
What you see here is daily life,
but twisted in strange ways.

17:24.400 --> 17:29.730
A broken peace, where what should not 
be normal has long since become so.

17:30.330 --> 17:33.520
The madness has spread 
all the way back home.

17:33.520 --> 17:36.480
Or did you think it was
 only the front lines...

17:36.480 --> 17:39.290
...that destroyed one's humanity?

17:39.290 --> 17:42.010
All logic in the world 
has been destroyed,

17:42.010 --> 17:44.120
and chaos continues to grow stronger.

17:44.660 --> 17:48.170
And so they seek a greater being.

17:48.530 --> 17:50.430
They seek faith.

17:51.710 --> 17:55.290
<i>Everyone you see is afraid.</i>

18:03.200 --> 18:08.610
The coffins of the war dead 
are a part of daily life now.

18:08.940 --> 18:14.060
Zettour would've likely called it 
the omnipresence of death.

18:15.220 --> 18:18.890
But we can see hope, too.

18:19.330 --> 18:20.350
What?

18:20.350 --> 18:23.220
The people's lack of overt emotion

18:23.220 --> 18:26.610
is proof that they still care 
about the national interest.

18:26.610 --> 18:29.110
We are modern men and women.

18:29.110 --> 18:32.890
If we have logical discussions, 
based on the principles of free will...

18:32.250 --> 18:34.000
Are you stupid?

18:36.170 --> 18:38.100
You are stupid.

18:38.470 --> 18:40.740
Use your damn head.

18:40.740 --> 18:43.040
And get back your common sense.

18:43.390 --> 18:47.890
When anger goes too far, 
it turns into calm.

18:47.890 --> 18:51.980
Someone who's crossed their boiling point
 can actually seem restrained.

18:52.320 --> 18:54.660
While you have the strength 
to scream, you scream.

18:55.060 --> 18:59.310
But once you've hit the bottom 
and lack that vigor...

18:59.620 --> 19:03.810
So you're saying this quiet 
itself is dangerous?

19:03.810 --> 19:05.030
Yes.

19:05.470 --> 19:09.840
The capital is a powder keg 
that's about to explode.

19:11.040 --> 19:14.590
The Empire itself is 
trapped in purgatory.

19:15.320 --> 19:19.160
Lieutenant Colonel, public opinion is 
a dangerous thing when it's inflamed.

19:19.650 --> 19:21.350
More than any monster.

19:22.180 --> 19:24.910
<i>Yes, if we ignore public opinion,</i>

19:24.910 --> 19:29.190
<i>there'll be chaos after 
the war even if we win.</i>

19:29.720 --> 19:33.430
<i>Public opinion is something 
I'll never understand, in any era.</i>

19:34.100 --> 19:39.060
Then that's all the more reason 
that we have to do our jobs.

19:39.450 --> 19:40.850
For peace.

19:42.390 --> 19:46.110
I didn't know you loved peace so much.

19:46.540 --> 19:48.370
I'm a coward, you see.

19:48.650 --> 19:51.910
A coward? You?

19:51.910 --> 19:53.450
That's a surprise.

19:53.450 --> 19:55.630
You could write a fairy tale about that.

19:55.630 --> 20:00.550
I'll ask Strategic HQ to publish it.
Please share the royalties.

20:00.550 --> 20:03.150
Royalties, you say?

20:03.990 --> 20:06.420
Very well. I'll promise you that.

20:06.940 --> 20:12.080
If we can end this war, I'll make a 
picture book out of what you just said.

20:12.080 --> 20:14.680
What an honor.

20:15.350 --> 20:18.560
We could title it... Hmm...

20:19.010 --> 20:22.550
How do you like "The Cowardly Hero"?

20:36.330 --> 20:39.340
At the Eastern Front,
Soldiers Enjoy Hot Meat and Soup

20:39.330 --> 20:41.720
Total bullshit.

20:41.720 --> 20:45.340
I thought part of propaganda was writing 
something people would believe.

20:45.340 --> 20:49.100
Absolute Victory Over
 Allied Kingdom Fleet

20:45.890 --> 20:48.450
<i>Everyone wants to believe in a dream.</i>

20:49.100 --> 20:53.850
The Empire's Mages are the Strongest in the World!
 The Day of Total Victory is Nigh!

20:49.710 --> 20:52.890
<i>A great victory for the great Empire.</i>

20:54.080 --> 20:57.360
<i>To be honest, it makes me 
feel like I'm going crazy.</i>

21:05.360 --> 21:09.860
Not everyone can live 
their lives the way you do.

21:09.860 --> 21:12.150
You are stupid.

21:12.150 --> 21:14.270
Use your damn head.

21:14.730 --> 21:17.200
And get back your common sense.

21:18.230 --> 21:21.750
<i>No, maybe I'm the crazy one.</i>

21:23.210 --> 21:27.510
<i>Until now, my goal has been to live 
a civilized life in the rear.</i>

21:27.960 --> 21:32.220
<i>But as long as the Empire is like this,
that won't happen here.</i>

21:32.900 --> 21:36.550
<i>Being X, you fucker, you're going to pay</i>

21:37.170 --> 21:39.910
<i>for throwing me into this 
shithole of a world.</i>

23:14.290 --> 23:18.050
Wh-What is this?

23:18.460 --> 23:21.900
General Rudersdorf asked us to find 
an outfit that would make it look like

23:21.900 --> 23:23.840
